ekly demo, one named lead, one line of accountability", "Scope and exit criteria written before anyone starts"], "note": "Ends when the scope ends. No minimum term beyond it.", "arm": "delivery"}, "handover": {"n": "Build, operate, transfer", "t": "4\u201318 months", "p": "Build + operate", "h": "Fixed price", "l": "A team in India that becomes yours. We hire it against your scorecard, run it while it matures, and transfer it to your entity on a date agreed in the contract.", "pts": ["<b>Build</b> \u2014 hired against your criteria, not a generic offshore standard", "<b>Operate</b> \u2014 we run delivery, payroll and compliance while it matures", "<b>Transfer</b> \u2014 people, contracts and knowledge move to your entity", "The transfer date is written in from day one, not negotiated later", "Your own leadership embedded through the operate phase", "Retention through transfer is the number we are measured on"], "note": "The usual route into India for teams not ready to open an entity yet.", "arm": "delivery"}, "diligence": {"n": "Technical due diligence", "t": "2\u20133 weeks", "p": "Fixed fee", "h": "Fixed price", "l": "An assessment of a target company's engineering team and codebase, written for people who will act on it.", "pts": ["The team assessed against the same scorecard we use on candidates", "Architecture, delivery cadence and operational maturity", "Key-person risk named, with who and why", "What it would cost to fix, in order of what it costs to ignore"], "note": "Built for private equity and corp-dev timelines. No hiring attached.", "arm": "delivery"}, "teamread": {"n": "Team assessment", "t": "2 weeks", "p": "Fixed fee", "h": "Fixed price", "l": "Your existing team, assessed against the standard you would hire to today.", "pts": ["Each person assessed against the same six to eleven criteria", "Where the team is strong, thin, and duplicated", "What your next three hires should actually be", "Individual feedback shared with each person, not only with you"], "note": "Uncomfortable, useful, and the individual feedback is non-negotiable.", "arm": "delivery"}};
